<ul>
    <li><strong>SessionStart</strong> — when a session starts. OMC initialization, loading notepad · project-memory, recovering the state of the mode that ran just before.</li>
    <li><strong>UserPromptSubmit</strong> — when you send a prompt. Magic keyword detection, automatically wiring up the right skill, context injection.</li>
    <li><strong>PreToolUse</strong> — just before using a tool. Hints recommending parallel reads, suggestions to preload related files.</li>
    <li><strong>PostToolUse</strong> — just after using a tool. Result verification, suggestions for follow-up action, suggestions for automatic fixes when an error is detected.</li>
</ul>

<h4>Reading the messages you see mid-conversation</h4>
<p>While working you may see messages in the form of <code>system-reminder</code>. Don't be alarmed — just understand them as below.</p>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>hook success: Success</code></td><td>A sign that it is working normally. You can just go on.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>hook additional context: ...</code></td><td>A useful hint. It is good to take it into account and apply it.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>[MAGIC KEYWORD: ralph detected]</code></td><td>A notice that the corresponding mode (here, ralph) has been turned on automatically.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>The boulder never stops rolling</code></td><td>A sign that ralph · ultrawork is still running.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h4>Memory and project documentation</h4>
<p>OMC provides three mechanisms for keeping the work context even across sessions. Each differs in where it is stored and what it does.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>deepinit</strong> — skims the whole codebase and creates an <code>AGENTS.md</code> document in each directory. It lays out what each folder holds, the relationships between files, things to watch out for while working, and dependencies, so the AI does not have to explore the structure from scratch every time. It is useful as preparatory groundwork on large projects.</li>
    <li><strong>notepad</strong> — a work memo stored in <code>.omc/notepad.md</code>. It survives even when the conversation gets long and the context is compacted. It is divided into three tiers — information you must never lose (priority), the state of the work currently in progress (working), and memos you record manually (manual) — and cleaning up old items is handled with the notepad_prune tool.</li>
    <li><strong>project memory</strong> — stored in <code>.omc/project-memory.json</code>, it remembers the project's tech stack, coding conventions, and architecture guidelines. The defaults are set with <code>omc-setup</code>.</li>
</ul>
<pre><code><span class="c"># Analyze the codebase and generate a per-directory AGENTS.md document (current path if [path] is omitted)</span>
/oh-my-claudecode:deepinit [path]</code></pre>
